    // --- sentinels for reproducibility. These four were caught disagreeing with a baseline that had just been
    //     generated from them, in the same code and on the same machine - only under a different test filter.
    //     "Repeat" turns that into something the suite notices by itself instead of by accident.
    //
    //     2026-09-02: a survey with Defaults.Repeat = 3 over all cases (8 minutes) found six that do not
    //     reproduce within one run - DifferenceBug9, DifferenceBug14, DifferenceBug15, UniteBug1, UniteBug6,
    //     UniteBug7. UniteBug4 and UniteBug5 came out stable in that survey but keep their Repeat: they were
    //     seen to move before, and three runs cannot prove stability, only disprove it. For the same reason
    //     the list below is a lower bound - a case that flickers one run in five can pass a survey of three.
    {
      "Name": "DifferenceBug14",
      "Status": "Ok",
      "Repeat": 3,
      "Comment": "found unstable by the 2026-09-02 survey; both shells move between runs"
    },
    {
      "Name": "UniteBug1",
      "Status": "Ok",
